                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the commercial operating model`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Thornbury's three largest accounts (£19M, 13% of revenue) have mandated punch-out catalogues, real-time stock/ETA, self-service reordering and API integration from <strong>1 October 2026</strong>, and Thornbury can meet none of those requirements today. Another ~£22M of mid-market accounts are watching, so <strong>~28% of revenue (~£41M)</strong> is exposed within 12 months. Of the 95 field reps, 18 are digitally confident and 41 actively resist. Around the table there are four theories of what this problem is. Choose yours, name the accounts that are most exposed, and decide how hard you treat the deadline.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Sequence the £4.5M roadmap`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Allocate the <strong>£4.5M</strong> across four levers: commerce platform and e-procurement, CRM and analytics, rep reskilling and change, and the inside-sales/digital channel. Full scope costs <strong>~£7.8M (1.7× the budget)</strong>, so something is deferred. The mandate date is 1 October, and the people who will sell through the new tools are the same 95 reps. Publish the allocation and say what comes first and what waits.`,
